# American spelling

Write American English in prose, comments, UI copy, reports, and identifiers.

- colour → color (colours, colored, coloring)
- centre → center (centered, centering)
- grey → gray
- disc → disk, for the solar disk and similar
- neighbour → neighbor
- normalise → normalize, summarise → summarize, and the same -ise / -isation ending when the American form is -ize / -ization

```text
Bad:  "the disc colour at the centre"
Good: "the disk color at the center"
```

Leave the original spelling of cited titles and proper names. Leave abbreviations that are not the word, such as a discriminant named `disc`.
